1
00:02:09,580 --> 00:02:16,560
Please welcome to the stage CEO of Google Cloud, Thomas Kurian.

2
00:02:34,785 --> 00:02:35,660
Hello.

3
00:02:43,900 --> 00:02:46,900
Welcome everyone to Google Cloud Next.

4
00:02:46,900 --> 00:02:53,580
Just one year ago, we stood on this same stage and promised a new future for AI.

5
00:02:53,580 --> 00:03:00,940
Today, that future is running in production at a scale that the world has never seen.

6
00:03:00,940 --> 00:03:05,060
Over the last year, we didn't just see adoption.

7
00:03:05,060 --> 00:03:07,660
We saw transformation.

8
00:03:07,660 --> 00:03:15,180
Nearly 75% of Google Cloud customers now leverage our AI products to power their businesses.

9
00:03:15,180 --> 00:03:20,260
We have thousands of agents and services across every industry,

10
00:03:20,260 --> 00:03:25,460
reaching billions of people through the global scale of our partner network.

11
00:03:25,460 --> 00:03:28,860
You have moved beyond the pilot.

12
00:03:28,860 --> 00:03:31,660
The experimenting phase is behind us.

13
00:03:31,660 --> 00:03:34,460
And now, the real challenge begins.

14
00:03:34,460 --> 00:03:40,860
How do you move AI into production across your entire enterprise?

15
00:03:40,860 --> 00:03:43,340
The answer is a unified stack.

16
00:03:43,340 --> 00:03:51,380
You cannot deliver AI by piecing together a puzzle piece of fragmented silicon and disconnected models.

17
00:03:51,380 --> 00:03:58,930
To drive real value, you need an architecture where chips are designed for the models,

18
00:03:58,930 --> 00:04:09,130
models are grounded in your data, agents and applications are built with models and secured by the infrastructure.

19
00:04:09,130 --> 00:04:23,290
Google uses this exact same OpenStack to reimagine how we serve users using our AI tools across Search, YouTube, Chrome, and Android.

20
00:04:23,290 --> 00:04:28,290
To take you inside that journey, let's hear from Sundar Pichai.

21
00:04:32,210 --> 00:04:34,730
Thanks, Thomas, and hello, everyone.

22
00:04:34,730 --> 00:04:37,010
We are so glad you are here.

23
00:04:37,010 --> 00:04:44,890
The pace of technological change has been faster than I've ever seen, and I've been around technology for a while.

24
00:04:44,890 --> 00:04:52,080
In fact, this Sunday, I'm celebrating my Googleversary-- 22 years, and I'm still feeling lucky.

25
00:04:52,080 --> 00:04:56,280
And I hope that luck extends to all of you in Vegas this week.

26
00:04:56,280 --> 00:05:00,960
I was drawn to Google all those years ago because of its ambitious mission.

27
00:05:00,960 --> 00:05:09,000
From the web to mobile to AI, every platform shift has given us new opportunities to advance our mission

28
00:05:09,000 --> 00:05:13,840
and to help our customers and partners achieve yours.

29
00:05:13,840 --> 00:05:18,480
As we move into the agentic era, we are taking this to the next level.

30
00:05:18,480 --> 00:05:22,560
We are making big investments now and for the future.

31
00:05:22,560 --> 00:05:27,280
In 2022, we were investing $31 billion in CapEx.

32
00:05:27,280 --> 00:05:38,360
This year, we plan to invest between $175 to $185 billion in total CapEx, a nearly 6x increase in just four years.

33
00:05:38,360 --> 00:05:47,880
And for 2026, just over half of our machine learning compute is expected to go towards the cloud business, so it will greatly benefit all of you.

34
00:05:47,880 --> 00:05:55,510
These investments are how we continue to stay at the frontier and ensure you're at the cutting edge as well.

35
00:05:55,510 --> 00:06:03,150
A big focus for us is to always be customer 0 for our own technologies, so we can be a better partner to all of you.

36
00:06:03,150 --> 00:06:08,870
Let me share a few examples of how we are rewiring our work with AI.

37
00:06:08,870 --> 00:06:14,830
First, coding-- we've been using AI to generate code internally at Google for a while.

38
00:06:14,830 --> 00:06:23,910
Today, nearly 75% of all new code at Google is AI-generated and approved by engineers, up from 50% last fall.

39
00:06:23,910 --> 00:06:27,830
We are now shifting to truly agentic workflows.

40
00:06:27,830 --> 00:06:37,590
Our engineers are orchestrating fully autonomous digital task forces, firing off agents, and accomplishing incredible things.

41
00:06:37,590 --> 00:06:45,350
As one example of how we are using agents, we recently executed a particularly complex code migration.

42
00:06:45,350 --> 00:06:50,020
Anyone familiar knows these migrations can take a while to get done.

43
00:06:50,020 --> 00:06:58,220
We created a system of agents taking on three different types of roles-- planners, orchestrators, and coders.

44
00:06:58,220 --> 00:07:04,980
Working together with engineers, we completed the migration 6x faster than we could have a year ago.

45
00:07:04,980 --> 00:07:13,140
And now we are applying that approach across our entire development cycle, from experimentation to testing to evals.

46
00:07:13,140 --> 00:07:17,660
It's not just developers who are infusing AI into their workflows.

47
00:07:17,660 --> 00:07:23,340
Our marketing teams are fundamentally rethinking the creative process from concept to launch.

48
00:07:23,340 --> 00:07:28,500
Historically, adapting a campaign for every audience, channel, and country took weeks.

49
00:07:28,500 --> 00:07:37,300
For the recent launch of Gemini and Chrome, teams used our models to rapidly generate thousands of variations of our creative assets.

50
00:07:37,300 --> 00:07:41,180
This enabled personalization at a massive scale.

51
00:07:41,180 --> 00:07:47,020
It also led to 70% faster turnaround and a 20% increase in conversion.

52
00:07:47,020 --> 00:07:49,420
We are not only getting to market faster.

53
00:07:49,420 --> 00:07:52,820
We are also doing it more effectively with AI.

54
00:07:52,820 --> 00:07:57,100
Our security teams are also seeing significant gains with AI.

55
00:07:57,100 --> 00:08:07,100
Each month, our teams receive unstructured threat reports at a scale that would take thousands of hours to review-- a nearly impossible task.

56
00:08:07,100 --> 00:08:15,940
Today, our Security Operations Center agents automatically triage tens of thousands of unstructured threat reports each month.

57
00:08:15,940 --> 00:08:24,980
By accelerating the extraction of critical intelligence and filtering out the noise, it's reduced threat mitigation time by over 90%

58
00:08:24,980 --> 00:08:28,540
We are more on the front foot than ever before.

59
00:08:28,540 --> 00:08:31,980
Those are just a few examples of what we are trying at Google.

60
00:08:31,980 --> 00:08:35,260
We are moving in a bold and responsible way.

61
00:08:35,260 --> 00:08:37,220
There's a lot of change happening.

62
00:08:37,220 --> 00:08:40,980
And it can feel like we are in the messy part of the innovation cycle.

63
00:08:40,980 --> 00:08:48,050
But we are starting to see the foundational building blocks coming together, unlocking a new wave of innovation.

64
00:08:48,050 --> 00:08:53,730
One thing that is super clear-- we are firmly in the agentic Gemini era.

65
00:08:53,730 --> 00:09:00,410
Last fall, we introduced Gemini Enterprise as a front door to agentic AI in the workplace.

66
00:09:00,410 --> 00:09:08,050
What we have seen in just a few months since launch is how every employee in every organization can become a builder.

67
00:09:08,050 --> 00:09:10,290
This is an incredible shift.

68
00:09:10,290 --> 00:09:15,730
We are accomplishing bigger things faster, but this comes with complexity.

69
00:09:15,730 --> 00:09:22,370
The conversation has gone from can we build an agent to how do we manage thousands of them?

70
00:09:22,370 --> 00:09:28,370
Today, I'm excited to announce our new Gemini Enterprise Agent Platform.

71
00:09:28,370 --> 00:09:38,970
It provides the secure, full-stack connective tissue you need to build, scale, govern, and optimize your agents with confidence.

72
00:09:38,970 --> 00:09:48,240
Think of it as mission control for the agentic enterprise to help move your organization into the next phase of the agentic era.

73
00:09:48,240 --> 00:09:51,240
I'm going to turn it back over to Thomas to share more.

74
00:09:51,240 --> 00:09:54,440
But first, thanks again for being here.

75
00:09:54,440 --> 00:10:01,840
Together, we are building a blueprint for true business transformation, and I'm excited to see where it takes us next.

76
00:10:01,840 --> 00:10:05,212
Thomas, back to you.

77
00:10:20,280 --> 00:10:22,000
Thank you, Sundar.

78
00:10:22,000 --> 00:10:29,040
Today, we're taking the next step in bringing Google AI to every employee and every workflow.

79
00:10:29,040 --> 00:10:38,640
Gemini Enterprise is now the end-to-end system for the agentic era, the connective tissue between your data, your people, and your goals.

80
00:10:38,640 --> 00:10:43,550
It transforms disconnected processes into a single intelligent flow.

81
00:10:43,550 --> 00:10:47,590
This is our blueprint for the agentic enterprise.

82
00:10:47,590 --> 00:10:51,470
It's also the answer to that fundamental question.

83
00:10:51,470 --> 00:10:56,590
Intelligence plus automation must deliver value.

84
00:10:56,590 --> 00:11:01,350
To make this work, you need context and action.

85
00:11:01,350 --> 00:11:04,030
Intelligence comes from your data.

86
00:11:04,030 --> 00:11:06,870
Automation is driven by agents.

87
00:11:06,870 --> 00:11:13,030
To solve this equation at scale, you need a complete integrated system.

88
00:11:13,030 --> 00:11:23,710
Today, we will show you the layers of that system and all the innovations we're introducing at every layer, starting with the AI Hypercomputer,

89
00:11:23,710 --> 00:11:29,790
the purpose-built foundation optimized for the physics of the agentic era;

90
00:11:29,790 --> 00:11:40,340
the Agentic Data Cloud, the engine that provides agents with trusted business context; Agentic Defense, the autonomous

91
00:11:40,340 --> 00:11:45,060
protection that secures your entire AI lifecycle;

92
00:11:45,060 --> 00:11:53,340
the Agentic Platform, the system to build, deploy, and manage agents; and finally, the Agentic Task

93
00:11:53,340 --> 00:12:02,100
Force, the pre-built specialized agents that we offer that are ready to transform your business.

94
00:12:02,100 --> 00:12:03,980
Let's dive in.

95
00:12:03,980 --> 00:12:14,180
Now, the Gemini Enterprise Agent platform is the environment where your business logic, your data, and your models converge to drive autonomous action.

96
00:12:14,180 --> 00:12:22,180
It expands on the previous capabilities of Vertex AI and brings new capabilities to enable your teams

97
00:12:22,180 --> 00:12:32,620
to build, scale, govern, and optimize agents with the same architectural rigor you apply to your most mission-critical systems.

98
00:12:32,620 --> 00:12:37,820
At its core, we build on our support for state-of-the-art models.

99
00:12:37,820 --> 00:12:42,980
Our most advanced reasoning model, Gemini 3.1 Pro, is available in preview.

100
00:12:42,980 --> 00:12:46,300
It's optimized for complex workflow orchestration.

101
00:12:46,300 --> 00:12:54,340
It bridges the gap between strategy and autonomous execution, interacting with your APIs and systems with minimal tuning.

102
00:12:54,340 --> 00:13:01,700
Industry leaders, including Databricks, JetBrains, and Replit, have chosen Gemini 3.1 Pro.

103
00:13:01,700 --> 00:13:06,060
We're also announcing Gemini 3.1 Flash Image,

104
00:13:06,060 --> 00:13:11,380
also known as Nano Banana 2, for high-fidelity visual assets;

105
00:13:11,380 --> 00:13:16,940
Veo 3.1 Lite, our most cost-effective video model,

106
00:13:16,940 --> 00:13:20,340
designed to build high-volume video applications;

107
00:13:20,340 --> 00:13:30,380
and Lyria 3 Pro, a state-of-the-art model for enterprise and professional-grade audio and music.

108
00:13:30,380 --> 00:13:33,740
All of these models are available in preview.

109
00:13:33,740 --> 00:13:41,570
Finally, we support all the leading models from Anthropic, including Claude Opus, Sonnet, and Haiku.

110
00:13:41,570 --> 00:13:47,690
And today, we're adding support for Anthropic's Claude Opus 4.7.

111
00:13:47,690 --> 00:13:59,090
While all of these models represent a massive leap in intelligence, their true value is realized when they're operationalized to solve mission-critical problems.

112
00:13:59,090 --> 00:14:07,330
Earlier this year, we announced a monumental partnership with one of the world's most iconic brands,

113
00:14:07,330 --> 00:14:12,130
that will bring the power of our technology to users everywhere around the world.

114
00:14:12,130 --> 00:14:22,290
We're collaborating with Apple as their preferred cloud provider to develop the next generation of Apple foundation models based on Gemini technology.

115
00:14:22,290 --> 00:14:33,930
These models will help power future Apple Intelligence features, including a more personalized Siri coming later this year.

116
00:14:33,930 --> 00:14:38,680
Leading organizations aren't just using Gemini Enterprise to work faster.

117
00:14:38,680 --> 00:14:43,080
They're using it to redefine what their businesses can do.

118
00:14:43,080 --> 00:14:47,440
Citi Wealth, in partnership with Google Cloud and DeepMind,

119
00:14:47,440 --> 00:14:56,800
today unveiled Citi Sky, an always-on AI-powered member of the Citi Wealth team that brings

120
00:14:56,800 --> 00:15:03,080
Citi's global intelligence to clients' fingertips.

121
00:15:03,080 --> 00:15:06,240
Citi Sky will provide an exemplary experience,

122
00:15:06,240 --> 00:15:15,680
allowing clients and colleagues to ask more of Citi Wealth whenever they need it, and in multiple languages.

123
00:15:15,680 --> 00:15:25,760
Honeywell generates billions of insights for managing buildings by training digital twins on over a million product specifications.

124
00:15:25,760 --> 00:15:36,990
Liverpool is bringing their signature in-store service online, projecting a 10 times return on investment on their new shopping assistant.

125
00:15:36,990 --> 00:15:42,110
And for a mission that's quite literally out of this world,

126
00:15:42,110 --> 00:15:45,670
we were very proud to partner with NASA--

127
00:15:53,950 --> 00:16:03,510
--to use Gemini Enterprise Agents to power flight readiness and ensure astronaut safety for Artemis II, which

128
00:16:03,510 --> 00:16:09,390
set the human spaceflight record for traveling the furthest distance from Earth.

129
00:16:09,390 --> 00:16:15,270
Now, we built the agent platform to manage the entire lifecycle of an agent.

130
00:16:15,270 --> 00:16:22,870
The low-code Agent Studio enables every employee to build and deploy agents using natural language.

131
00:16:22,870 --> 00:16:33,340
It grounds LLM reasoning in your specific business rules, bringing predictable, autonomous action to every workflow at scale.

132
00:16:33,340 --> 00:16:39,740
To manage these assets, the agent registry provides a single point of control,

133
00:16:39,740 --> 00:16:47,860
indexing every internal agent and tool across your organization to ensure they're discoverable and governed.

134
00:16:47,860 --> 00:16:58,020
Similarly, our Skills and Tools Registry allows you to define modular, reusable packages of instructions, scripts, and resources

135
00:16:58,020 --> 00:17:04,380
to teach agents to perform specialized tasks or repeatable workflows.

136
00:17:04,380 --> 00:17:14,180
We also expose skills for every GCP service and every service in Workspace in our skills registry.

137
00:17:14,180 --> 00:17:18,460
All of this is also supported by our Agent Marketplace,

138
00:17:18,460 --> 00:17:31,920
allowing you to search and deploy specialized agents from our global partner ecosystem directly in Gemini Enterprise, including Atlassian, Box,

139
00:17:31,920 --> 00:17:38,460
Lovable, Oracle, ServiceNow, Workday, and many, many more.

140
00:17:38,460 --> 00:17:49,700
Finally, with our native integration of Model Context Protocol, or MCP, you can connect our agent platform to any MCP server.

141
00:17:49,700 --> 00:18:01,220
We're also exposing all of our GCP services as MCP to allow you to interact seamlessly with GCP from any agent.

142
00:18:01,220 --> 00:18:11,380
In addition to developing this agent platform, it also provides the framework to orchestrate and scale your entire agentic workforce.

143
00:18:11,380 --> 00:18:14,860
We enable agent-to-agent orchestration,

144
00:18:14,860 --> 00:18:27,810
allowing agents to seamlessly delegate tasks from one to another, including support for complex generative and deterministic orchestration patterns.

145
00:18:27,810 --> 00:18:34,850
This helps ensure that for your critical workflows, such as those that need compliance,

146
00:18:34,850 --> 00:18:44,010
your agents can follow well-specified paths every single time, guaranteeing predictable outcomes.

147
00:18:44,010 --> 00:18:47,610
Orchestration flows and agents can respond to events.

148
00:18:47,610 --> 00:18:49,730
These events can be real-time.

149
00:18:49,730 --> 00:18:51,890
They can be schedule-based.

150
00:18:51,890 --> 00:18:56,690
They can be trigger-based, or they can be batch inference job.

151
00:18:56,690 --> 00:19:04,490
We're bringing zero-trust verification to every agent and every orchestration step.

152
00:19:04,490 --> 00:19:15,810
And now with Agent Identity, every agent has a unique cryptographic ID and well-defined authorization

153
00:19:15,810 --> 00:19:19,290
policies that are traceable and auditable,

154
00:19:19,290 --> 00:19:27,680
ensuring you can track every action in your company and manage all your agents.

155
00:19:27,680 --> 00:19:38,360
They're also centrally managed through our Agent Gateway, which provides a single command center for policy enforcement across the organization.

156
00:19:38,360 --> 00:19:42,240
Paired with Model Armor, you protect your models.

157
00:19:42,240 --> 00:19:49,040
You protect your proprietary enterprise data from threats such as sensitive data leakage.

158
00:19:49,040 --> 00:19:57,840
This integrated approach, from secure sandboxes to a single management console, provides the visibility

159
00:19:57,840 --> 00:20:06,320
and isolation you need to run your most-sensitive workloads with a high degree of confidence.

160
00:20:06,320 --> 00:20:12,400
Now, optimization and observability are also built into the fabric of the platform.

161
00:20:12,400 --> 00:20:25,070
Agent observability delivers granular instrumentation, allowing you to visualize the full execution path of any agent using OTel-compliant telemetry.

162
00:20:25,070 --> 00:20:33,910
You can retrieve traces, monitor tool use, quickly diagnose reasoning loops with fine-grained logging.

163
00:20:33,910 --> 00:20:37,470
All of these capabilities that we've just detailed--

164
00:20:37,470 --> 00:20:46,430
the orchestration, zero-trust security, and developer tools-- form the core engine of Gemini Enterprise.

165
00:20:46,430 --> 00:20:58,510
While the agent platform is where your technical teams build and govern agent, the Gemini Enterprise application is the primary environment where your business actually operates.

166
00:20:58,510 --> 00:21:10,310
It's that new front door to AI for all your employees, turning complex agentic capabilities into a simple, new way to work for every employee.

167
00:21:10,310 --> 00:21:17,630
By unifying data across your entire stack, including Google Workspace, coding tools,

168
00:21:17,630 --> 00:21:24,740
and enterprise systems, we've created a single intelligent flow for the entire organization.

169
00:21:24,740 --> 00:21:32,220
To give your teams a permanent memory, we're introducing Gemini Enterprise projects.

170
00:21:32,220 --> 00:21:45,020
Projects give your agents a high-fidelity workspace and the ability to use deep think to solve your most complex business challenges without context pollution.

171
00:21:45,020 --> 00:21:56,460
We're also adding Microsoft 365 interoperability, allowing you to export the Docs and Slides you've created within Canvas into common Microsoft Office formats.

172
00:22:02,020 --> 00:22:07,460
Leading innovators already use this platform to redefine their industries.

173
00:22:07,460 --> 00:22:11,572
Let's hear from one of them, Virgin Voyages.

174
00:22:15,737 --> 00:22:17,820
Our people are a secret sauce.

175
00:22:17,820 --> 00:22:23,420
So anytime we can use data to make our people more empowered, we're all in.

176
00:22:23,420 --> 00:22:30,082
Gemini Enterprise is a front door for AI in our business, and we're using it to bring natural language intelligence to our crew.

177
00:22:30,082 --> 00:22:33,760
Gemini Enterprise is helping us bring Project 3D to life.

178
00:22:33,760 --> 00:22:38,240
It's going to allow our crew to feel confident with any question they're asked.

179
00:22:38,240 --> 00:22:44,420
So for sailors, Rovey is a personal concierge to maximize the value they get out of their vacation,

180
00:22:44,420 --> 00:22:50,380
inspired at home all the way through the last day of their voyage to make sure they have the best time on vacation with us.

181
00:22:50,380 --> 00:22:55,860
Our crew are already world-renowned and award-winning for the exceptional service they deliver as humans.

182
00:22:55,860 --> 00:23:00,420
We want Project 3D and Gemini Enterprise to be able to take that even further.

183
00:23:00,420 --> 00:23:05,260
So you can imagine when you're building something for a cruise ship, there are challenges that pop up.

184
00:23:05,260 --> 00:23:08,500
There's not exactly a fiber cable running out the back of the ship.

185
00:23:08,500 --> 00:23:13,280
With Google Distributed Cloud Edge, we had data resiliency at the core of the project.

186
00:23:13,280 --> 00:23:17,860
And that means, even when we're offline, our intelligence is still online.

187
00:23:17,860 --> 00:23:24,790
Using our AI stack in Google Cloud has helped us not only reduce our production timeline by up to 60%,

188
00:23:24,790 --> 00:23:31,930
but we have contributed to a 28% increase month on month for a record sales quarter.

189
00:23:31,930 --> 00:23:41,575
We could truly see a day where you get on a Virgin Atlantic flight, stay at a Virgin hotel, and end up on a Virgin Voyage, all connected seamlessly by Project Ruby and Gemini Enterprise.

190
00:23:41,575 --> 00:23:44,450
Google has been a foundational partner for us.

191
00:23:44,450 --> 00:23:45,510
The extension of Gemini.

192
00:23:45,510 --> 00:23:48,230
Enterprise was the natural way to bring that mission to life.

193
00:23:58,290 --> 00:24:00,810
The era of the pilot is over.

194
00:24:00,810 --> 00:24:03,170
The era of the agent is here.

195
00:24:03,170 --> 00:24:07,610
But the true power comes from how it changes your workflow.

196
00:24:07,610 --> 00:24:09,410
Let's see it in action.

197
00:24:09,410 --> 00:24:11,890
Please welcome Erika Chuong.

198
00:24:21,920 --> 00:24:23,480
Thanks, Thomas.

199
00:24:23,480 --> 00:24:28,600
Gemini Enterprise is a platform to build, manage, and interact with agents.

200
00:24:28,600 --> 00:24:36,560
I'll demonstrate how it can orchestrate multiple agents across platforms, share context for seamless handoffs, and streamline workflows.

201
00:24:36,560 --> 00:24:39,720
Imagine I work for a global furniture retailer.

202
00:24:39,720 --> 00:24:49,120
Here's my personalized homepage where I can interact with internal business context and external sources in a single pane of glass.

203
00:24:49,120 --> 00:24:55,740
The agent gallery hosts my approved selection of agents, including built-in ones by Google and my company's agents,

204
00:24:55,740 --> 00:25:03,640
like this one for price and margin optimization, which autonomously orchestrates across agents, tools, and sources.

205
00:25:03,640 --> 00:25:07,480
Now, let's see Gemini Enterprise in action.

206
00:25:07,480 --> 00:25:14,780
To bring some less popular product lines back to life, we'll ask our agent to analyze current interior design trends,

207
00:25:14,780 --> 00:25:20,230
identify dead stock in our warehouse, and orchestrate a relaunch campaign.

208
00:25:20,230 --> 00:25:26,430
With that one prompt, multiple agents complete a series of actions in minutes instead of hours.

209
00:25:26,430 --> 00:25:36,230
My market research agent, powered by Deep Research, analyzes the latest Google Search information alongside my own sales and CSAT data.

